[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65456,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma (LCNEC) is a high-grade carcinoma composed of large cells with neuroendocrine differentiation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65457,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8013/3 Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65458,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C7Z &amp; XH0U20 Malignant neoplasms of female genital organs, unspecified &amp; Neuroendocrine carcinoma NOS</p>\r\n<p>2C7Z &amp; XH0NL5 Malignant neoplasms of female genital organs, unspecified &amp; Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65459,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> neuroendocrine carcinoma, large cell type</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> high-grade neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65460,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65461,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCNEC is rare in the female genital tract, but it most commonly arises in the cervix, followed by the endometrium, ovary, fallopian tube, vulva, and vagina {11993694}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65462,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Cervical and endometrial tumours usually present with abnormal vaginal bleeding; ovarian tumours present with symptoms related to an adnexal mass {21138780; 26945341; 19188820; 28735441; 29019870}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T09:09:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65463,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>LCNEC of the female genital tract is rare {29728073}. Cervical primaries typically affect premenopausal women (mean age: 34&nbsp;years), whereas endometrial and ovarian tumours affect perimenopausal and postmenopausal women {21138780; 26945341; 19188820; 28735441; 29019870}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T09:09:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65464,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cervical LCNEC is associated with high-risk HPV infection, most commonly with HPV18 {25661244}. The etiology of other gynaecological LCNECs is unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65465,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chromosome 3q gain or amplification has been detected in cervical LCNEC {16226109}. Defects in the mismatch repair system are common in endometrial LCNEC {26945341}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65466,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCNEC presents as a mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65467,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>LCNEC is composed of tumour cells with moderate amounts of cytoplasm and large nuclei with coarse chromatin and prominent nucleoli. There is typically an admixture of architectural patterns, including diffuse (which often predominates), trabecular, insular, pseudoglandular, and rosette-like. Numerous mitoses and areas of necrosis are common. Areas of small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma (SCNEC) or other histotypes may also be present {26945341; 19188820}. Ovarian LCNEC may be associated with teratoma {23091901}. Expression of at least one neuroendocrine marker (chromogranin, synaptophysin, or CD56) is necessary to establish the diagnosis. When CD56 is the only marker expressed, histological features typical of LCNEC must be present. Diffuse block-type p16 immunoreactivity, secondary to high-risk HPV, is common in cervical LCNECs but may also be observed in LCNEC at other sites. Detection of high-risk HPV may be useful in helping to confirm a cervical primary {20182342; 31263021}. Cases without neuroendocrine morphology should not be regarded as LCNEC even in the presence of neuroendocrine immunoreactivity. SMARCA4, SMARCA2, and SMARCB1 immunoreactivities are retained.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-04T16:21:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65468,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears from LCNEC show highly atypical cells with moderate to abundant cytoplasm, in groups and singly.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65469,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65470,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> high-grade neuroendocrine histomorphology with expression of at least one neuroendocrine marker.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65471,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is as for other carcinomas at the corresponding site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65472,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 407,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are aggressive neoplasms, with a high propensity for lymphatic and haematogenous spread. Distant metastasis at presentation is common. Mortality is high, even among patients diagnosed at an early stage {21138780}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-29T12:37:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]